# Build context of the backend image (root Dockerfile; docker-compose `app`).
# ALLOWLIST: only what the build stage compiles from may enter the context.
# The deploy checkout is a working tree: a local backend/dist (and
# node_modules, .env) accumulate there, and tsc never deletes an output whose
# source is gone — a dist/ringBuffer.js from a months-old local build rode
# into production this way (2026-11-06). Anything not listed below can no
# longer reach the image, whatever the host has. The session image builds
# from ./session-image, its own context; this file does not apply to it.
# CI's `backend-image` job proves it with a contaminated tree.
*
!backend/package.json
!backend/package-lock.json
!backend/tsconfig.json
!backend/src/
